.TH "FLOX\-PUSH" "1" "" "" "Flox User Manuals"
.SH NAME
flox\-push \- send environment to FloxHub
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.EX
flox [<general\-options>] push
     [\-d=<path>]
     [\-o=<owner>]
     [\-f]

flox [<general\-options>] push
     \-r=<owner>/<name>
     [\-f]
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Push an environment to FloxHub to share and centrally manage it with
flox, or sync changes made locally to a remote environment.
.PP
After pushing, the remote environment can be referred to as
\f[CR]<owner>/<name>\f[R].
.SS Pushing from a directory (using \f[CR]\-\-dir | \-d\f[R])
A path environment contains a manifest file and lock file which are
stored locally and possibly committed to version control.
Pushing the environment moves the manifest and lock file to FloxHub,
leaving a reference to the revision of the environment stored locally.
.PP
Once the environment has been pushed, it can be used directly with the
\f[CR]\-\-reference\f[R] option, or it can be used and edited locally
before syncing with \f[CR]flox push\f[R].
See \f[B]\f[CB]flox\-edit(1)\f[B]\f[R],
\f[B]\f[CB]flox\-install(1)\f[B]\f[R], and
\f[B]\f[CB]flox\-uninstall(1)\f[B]\f[R] for editing the environment.
.SS Pushing a remote environment (using \f[CR]\-\-reference | \-r\f[R])
When using the \f[CR]\-\-reference\f[R] flag, commands will operate on a
\f[B]central persistent local copy\f[R] of the environment.
Any changes made to an environment using the \f[CR]\-\-reference\f[R]
flag, affect only the local copy and must be explicitly updated on
FloxHub using \f[CR]flox push \-\-reference\f[R]
.SS Conflict resolution
In the same way as a git repo, local changes to an environment that has
been pushed may diverge from the environment on FloxHub if
\f[CR]flox push\f[R] is run from a different host.
Passing \f[CR]\-\-force\f[R] to \f[CR]flox push\f[R] will cause it to
overwrite any changes on FloxHub with local changes to the environment.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Push Options
.TP
\f[CR]\-d\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-dir\f[R]
Push an environment in a directory to FloxHub.
.RS
.PP
Cannot be used with \f[CR]\-\-reference\f[R].
Defaults to the current directory when \f[CR]\-\-reference\f[R] is not
specified.
.RE
.TP
\f[CR]\-o\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-owner\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-org\f[R]
FloxHub owner to push environment to (default: current FloxHub user).
.RS
.PP
Can only be specified when pushing an environment for the first time.
Use `flox pull \(encopy' to copy an existing environment and push it to
a new owner.
.PP
Cannot be used with \f[CR]\-\-reference\f[R].
.RE
.TP
\f[CR]\-r\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-reference\f[R]
Push local copy of a FloxHub environment upstream.
.RS
.PP
This pushes the local changes made to a FloxHub environment using
commands with the \f[CR]\-\-reference\f[R] flag.
Referring to environments, that have never been accessed or explicitly
pulled will cause an error.
.PP
Cannot be used with \f[CR]\-\-dir\f[R] or \f[CR]\-\-owner\f[R].
.RE
.TP
\f[CR]\-f\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-force\f[R]
Forcibly overwrite the remote copy of the environment.
.SS General Options
.TP
\f[CR]\-h\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-help\f[R]
Prints help information.
.PP
The following options can be passed when running any \f[CR]flox\f[R]
subcommand but must be specified \f[I]before\f[R] the subcommand.
.TP
\f[CR]\-v\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-verbose\f[R]
Increase logging verbosity.
Invoke multiple times for increasing detail.
.TP
\f[CR]\-q\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-quiet\f[R]
Silence logs except for errors.
